 Attempted rollback to v2.3.0, the most recent production release that was healthy, but it is quarantined for CVE-2026-4417 and the rollback was refused. (2) Rolled back checkout-api to v2.2.9, the most recent non-quarantined release that was healthy in production, in us-east, us-west and eu-west. v2.3.1 remains unhealthy and was not redeployed. Follow-up: verify checkout-api health and error rate after rollback; decide on a safe fix path for v2.3.1 and the handling of quarantined v2.3.0.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-sev2-v2.3.1-rollback-2026-05"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 17516, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01WvS2cHi9BZSf1snkHAq24A", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-sev2-v2.3.1-rollback-2026-05", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 17516, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01WvS2cHi9BZSf1snkHAq24A", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 19605, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "checkout-api is rolled back to v2.2.9 in all three regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west). It is healthy again, with an error rate of 0.002, down from 0.18 on v2.3.1.\n\n**Rollback deviation:** The rollback you asked for, to v2.3.0, was refused. v2.3.0 is quarantined for CVE-2026-4417. I used v2.2.9 instead, the next most recent production release that was healthy and is not quarantined. If you would rather not run v2.2.9, that needs a decision from you.\n\n**Incident:** I opened SEV2 incident INC-0001 for checkout-api, and it paged the on-call engineer. The summary covers the failed v2.3.0 rollback, the v2.2.9 rollback, and the follow-ups. The follow-ups are to verify health after the rollback and to decide on a fix path for v2.3.1 and the quarantined v2.3.0.\n\nv2.3.1 was not redeployed, and no change-manager approval was needed because v2.2.9 has been healthy in production.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_0193wDQjLk7vqcKXbisPyTKm", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01DbXJcCupSx5S3wyJZoM8c6", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The latest production release is v2.3.1, which is unhealthy. The most recent release that was healthy in production is v2.3.0. I'll roll back to it.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01M3i9ZGyhwb2uQMWK1WARyC", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "v2.3.0 is quarantined (CVE-2026-4417), so the rollback was refused. The next most recent production release that was healthy is v2.2.9, which is not quarantined. I'll roll back to that.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01ELgukzGynr6keENB3uZAfo", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.2.9"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01QfZh9juNMSL3pd22MmxKxp", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01WvS2cHi9BZSf1snkHAq24A", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api failing health checks after v2.3.1 deploy; rolled back to v2.2.9", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api began failing health checks after the v2.3.1 production deploy (error rate was 0.18 at time of check). Actions taken: (1) Attempted rollback to v2.3.0, the most recent production release that was healthy, but it is quarantined for CVE-2026-4417 and the rollback was refused. (2) Rolled back checkout-api to v2.2.9, the most recent non-quarantined release that was healthy in production, in us-east, us-west and eu-west. v2.3.1 remains unhealthy and was not redeployed. Follow-up: verify checkout-api health and error rate after rollback; decide on a safe fix path for v2.3.1 and the handling of quarantined v2.3.0.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-sev2-v2.3.1-rollback-2026-05"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "checkout-api is rolled back to v2.2.9 in all three regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west). It is healthy again, with an error rate of 0.002, down from 0.18 on v2.3.1.\n\n**Rollback deviation:** The rollback you asked for, to v2.3.0, was refused. v2.3.0 is quarantined for CVE-2026-4417. I used v2.2.9 instead, the next most recent production release that was healthy and is not quarantined. If you would rather not run v2.2.9, that needs a decision from you.\n\n**Incident:** I opened SEV2 incident INC-0001 for checkout-api, and it paged the on-call engineer. The summary covers the failed v2.3.0 rollback, the v2.2.9 rollback, and the follow-ups. The follow-ups are to verify health after the rollback and to decide on a fix path for v2.3.1 and the quarantined v2.3.0.\n\nv2.3.1 was not redeployed, and no change-manager approval was needed because v2.2.9 has been healthy in production.", "type": "text"}]}]}